The CS2 update of 2026-11-11 (2000943) removed the vtable from the registered
net message object. libnetworksystem now keeps one plain 0x28 byte struct per
message: name, an argument-less CNetMessage factory at 0x08, group name,
message id at 0x18, category masks, group id and flag bits at 0x25.
INetworkMessages::GetNetMessageInfo returns that pointer itself.

INetworkMessages shrank from 40 to 37 entries. SerializeAbstract,
AllocateAndCopyConstructNetMessageAbstract and DeallocateNetMessageAbstract
are gone, FindOrCreateNetMessage moved to index 20 and takes the factory, and
both unserialize entries gained an argument. FindNetworkMessagePartial was
still called through the old index 14, returned garbage, and the server
crashed in AllocateMessage() on startup. CNetMessage lost its GetName virtual.

INetworkMessageInternal is now NetMessageInfo_t plus non-virtual
GetUnscopedName, GetNetMessageInfo and AllocateMessage helpers, so callers
compile unchanged. Checked against libnetworksystem.so 2000943 (CNetworkMessages
vtable 0x4805d0) and the libserver.so TextMsg registration (0x17e273c).

scripts/build-steamrt3.sh applies this to its copy of hl2sdk bd17582. Drop it once the pinned
SDK commit declares the same layout.

